

class Solution {
    public String multiply(String num1, String num2) {

        // 🔹 Edge case: if any number is 0 → result is 0
        if (num1.equals("0") || num2.equals("0")) return "0";

        int n1 = num1.length();
        int n2 = num2.length();

        // 🔹 Result array to store multiplication result
        // Maximum length = n1 + n2
        int[] result = new int[n1 + n2];

        // 🔹 Traverse both strings from right to left
        for (int i = n1 - 1; i >= 0; i--) {

            for (int j = n2 - 1; j >= 0; j--) {

                // Convert char → int (e.g., '3' → 3)
                int digit1 = num1.charAt(i) - '0';
                int digit2 = num2.charAt(j) - '0';

                // Multiply digits
                int product = digit1 * digit2;

                // Positions in result array
                int pos1 = i + j;       // for carry
                int pos2 = i + j + 1;   // for actual digit

                // Add product to existing value at pos2
                int sum = product + result[pos2];

                // Store last digit at pos2
                result[pos2] = sum % 10;

                // Carry goes to pos1
                result[pos1] += sum / 10;
            }
        }

        // 🔹 Convert result array → string
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();

        for (int num : result) {

            // Skip leading zeros
            if (!(sb.length() == 0 && num == 0)) {
                sb.append(num);
            }
        }

        return sb.toString();
    }
}
🧠 Key Concept
We simulate manual multiplication
Each digit multiplies with every digit
Carry is handled using positions:
i + j → carry
i + j + 1 → actual digit
⏱️ Time Complexity
O(n1 × n2)
Two nested loops:
Outer loop → n1
Inner loop → n2

👉 So total operations = n1 × n2

📦 Space Complexity
O(n1 + n2)
Result array size = n1 + n2
🔥 Quick Summary
Part	Complexity
Time	O(n × m)
Space	O(n + m)
